class:: SpecPcile2
summary:: Generalized spectral percentile frequency
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/SpecPcile, Classes/SpecCentroid2, Classes/SpecFlatness2

description::
Finds the frequency below which the requested fraction of selected spectral weight lies. Optional within-bin interpolation avoids quantizing every answer to a bin center. Silence returns zero.

This is a non-destructive FFT reader. It is practically similar to link::Classes/SpecPcile:: and conventional spectral rolloff, but exposes the cumulative fraction, magnitude/power convention, bounds, interpolation, and units directly.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: chain
An FFT chain matching code::fftSize::.

argument:: fraction
Cumulative fraction from 0 through 1; 0.85 is a common rolloff value.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included frequency in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included frequency in Hz; 0 selects Nyquist.

argument:: interpolate
Nonzero enables linear location within the crossing bin.

argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 uses magnitude and 1 uses power.

argument:: fftSize
Literal FFT size from 256 through 8192.

returns::
Percentile frequency in Hz.

instancemethods::

examples::
The 85-percentile spectral rolloff tracks high-frequency energy distribution. In this example, it drives an adaptive exciter and sizzle gate: high-frequency bursts open an auxiliary ringing comb resonator, highlighting drum sizzle without muddying the low end. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: plots the rolloff boundary frequency in real time.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic drum fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
            var kick = SinOsc.ar(EnvGen.ar(Env([120, 45], [0.08], \exp), trig)) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.3), trig);
            var snare = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.15), Impulse.kr(2, 0.5));
            (kick + snare) * 0.5
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var rolloff = SpecPcile2.kr(chain, 0.85, fftSize: 1024);
        var sizzleOpen = (rolloff.clip(2000, 14000) / 14000).lag(0.04);
        var exciter = HPF.ar(source, 4000) * sizzleOpen * 0.4;
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + (exciter * 0.3);

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, rolloff) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Spectral Rolloff (85%)", ~miraBus, 500, 16000, "Hz");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
